  "body": "Closes #344\nCloses #322\nClaim: mac/verify-merges\n\nScreenshots of the Mac checks (the assertions of the local driver are the proof where a still frame cannot show a sequence) owed by cloud merges. Simulator, iOS 27.0, iPhone 18 Pro and iPad Pro 13-inch (M5), logged out (no pseudo, no account data). The checks were run on a dev-swift build at `34c4e556`, then again with the fix of #377, which is merged as `1c5cd6f`. A local XCUITest driver ran them. It is not committed, because the repo has no UI test target.\n\n| File | Check | Device | What it shows |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `344-1.png` | #344 row 2 | iPhone | Plus > Réglages > Icône opens its screen (with #377; on `34c4e556` the row highlighted and nothing opened) |\n| `344-2.png` | #344 row 2 | iPhone | Réglages again after the Icône round trips, a switch to Catégories and back to Plus (the frame shows only the end state; the sequence is in the written report on #344) |\n| `322-1.png` … `322-4.png` | #322 | iPhone | light, dark, Dynamic Type XL, AX5 (accessibility XXXL) |\n| `322-5.png` | #322 rotation | iPhone | rotation off, frame taken after landscape was requested: still portrait. The proof is the test's assertion on the window (height > width) |\n| `322-6.png` … `322-8.png` | #322 | iPad | light, dark, AX5 |\n| `322-9.png` | #322 | iPhone | at AX5 the Thème row (the issue's \"Apparence\" row) opens its screen |\n\niPad rotation (rotation off, landscape requested): the window turns landscape (test assertion width > height). There is no frame, because XCUITest draws a landscape iPad on a portrait canvas.\n\nThe per-row results are on #344 and #322. Rows 1a/1b of #344 drive a private conversation, so they have no screenshot.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFA3L8YfjJi4AdxgzW\n",
